{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And has not washed his hands in water.</b> While he has not immersed from his uncleanness — even if his flux has ceased and he counted seven and lacks only immersion — he conveys uncleanness through all his uncleannesses. And that the verse expressed immersion of the body of a zav in the language of washing of hands teaches you that concealed parts do not require entry of water, but only the exposed organ, like the hands (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:36.188017445Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}